cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Cohaera: passive security monitoring for AI agent telemetry"
message: >-
  If you use Cohaera in academic work, please cite it. Please also cite the
  version and the evaluation card digest: the numbers move between versions and
  a citation without them is not reproducible.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hafeez
    given-names: Imran
repository-code: "https://github.com/404SecNotFound/Cohaera"
abstract: >-
  Cohaera is a passive analyser for exported AI agent telemetry. It runs
  outside the agent's control path: it reconstructs sessions from JSONL
  events, verifies the integrity evidence those events carry, runs
  deterministic session-level detections, and emits security records that
  state what each check could and could not evaluate. It never decides
  whether an agent action may proceed. It has no runtime dependencies, works
  offline, and ships an evaluation card that reports its false-positive rate
  beside its recall together with a catalogue of the ways its checks can be
  defeated.
keywords:
  - agent security
  - LLM agents
  - detection engineering
  - telemetry
  - SIEM
  - prompt injection
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.3.0
